  "method": "This batch contains 31 fresh campaign cases, distinct from our earlier submissions: 10 improvements beyond the pinned current nominal/reference bounds and 21 improved complete certificates from physical source operations. Twenty certificate cases retain explicitly known nominal values; PR12L1.5/cube N24 conservatively claims only a reduced complete certificate. No new ideal bound is claimed for those 21 cases.\n\nThe constructions use marked cap exchanges and common separator returns, whole-child collar and height transfers, cross-base whole-prism inclusion and axial subdivision, complete prism self-host enclosure, and marked Catalan returns. Complete source owners, inherited author credits, frames, all host walls, pair separators, and the relevant common restoration paths are retained. The 75-dodecagonal-prism construction, for example, comes from 25 complete octagonal source prisms through a certified whole-envelope inclusion and three-child axial partition; its certified cube side is 10.834711256138021, below the retained bound of 11. Fixed-contact stress certificates and local frame results retain their stated scope; no global optimum is claimed.\n\nAll 31 packaged witnesses passed verify_general.py and certify_general.py (62 checks), independent complete geometry/source reviews, current public and retained-construction comparisons, and archive checksums/privacy/dependency checks. The trusted batch parser selects exactly 31 native candidates. Pinned comparison: repository 307ef472925069eabd9890cc38146f88dbdac9db and site build 2026-10-15 12:01. A further successor check passed at fe86acefe7a0b2d7092c241eecb772d914ae466b and site build 12:03. Acceptance and later site selection remain separate observations.\n\nThe archive retains all proof dependencies. Thirty-nine large proof companions are stored losslessly with gzip and an explicit original-path/hash restoration manifest; active native JSON witnesses remain directly readable. Original donors and classical mechanisms",
